.TH WOBBLY-CLOCK.CONF 5 "2026-11-04" "Wobbly Weathery Web Clock" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
wobbly\-clock.conf \- settings for wobbly\-clock
.SH DESCRIPTION
One setting per line, \fIkey = value\fR. Lines starting with # are comments. Only settings that differ from the default need to be written.
The keys and values are the web page's. A machine that cannot do a setting refuses it with the reason, and the clock uses the nearest setting it can.
.SH SETTINGS
.SS Clock
.TP
.B twentyFourHourClock
24\-hour time. Values: auto | on | off. Default: auto. null = follow the browser's locale until the user chooses.
.TP
.B hideSeconds
Hide seconds. Values: on | off. Default: off.
.TP
.B clockMode
The digits show (advanced). Values: time | countdown. Default: time. time | countdown: the digits show the time, or the time left to timerTarget.
.TP
.B timerTarget
Count down to (advanced). Values: yyyy\-mm\-ddThh:mm. Default: . countdown: a datetime\-local value ("2026\-12\-25T08:00"), in the viewer's own time zone.
.TP
.B timerLabel
Name (optional) (advanced). Values: text, up to 40 characters. Default: . countdown: a name shown with it.
.TP
.B clockStyle
Style. Values: auto | glass | stained | solid. Default: auto. auto (liquid glass; coloured tube from Thanksgiving to Christmas) | glass | stained (coloured tube) | solid. Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B glassFrost
Frosting. Values: 0 to 1. Default: 0.35. 0 clear .. 1 heavily frosted. Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B glassGlow
Light from inside. Values: 0 to 1. Default: 0. light from inside the glass, 0..1 (stained glass always glows a little). Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B legibility
Keep the time readable. Values: auto | high | off. Default: auto. off | auto (3:1) | high (4.5:1): least brightness contrast between the time and the sky.
.TP
.B glassGlowColor
Colour of the light (liquid glass) (advanced). Values: warm | white | cool | follow. Default: follow. liquid glass: warm | white | cool | follow (the sun / moon light). Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B clockColor
Ink colour (solid style) (advanced). Values: auto | classic | white. Default: auto. solid style only: auto | classic | white.
.SS Scene
.TP
.B landscape
Landscape. Values: auto | flat | hills | mountains | desert | ocean | city. Default: auto. auto (real terrain when available) | flat | ocean | hills | mountains | desert | city.
.TP
.B holidayTree
Christmas tree. Values: on | off. Default: on. a lit Christmas tree in the scene from Thanksgiving to Christmas. Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B plants
Plants that suit this place. Values: on | off. Default: on. grass, trees, cacti ... swaying in the wind. Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B quality
Quality (advanced). Values: auto | low | medium | high. Default: auto. auto | low | medium | high. Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi) and two or more cores.
.TP
.B detail
When the device is slow, keep (advanced). Values: auto | sharp | smooth. Default: auto. auto | sharp | smooth: what a device that cannot keep up gives up first. sharp keeps the picture at the display's size (sharp digits) and draws the sky and landscape smaller; smooth shrinks the whole picture (a small LED panel). Automatic: sharp on a display, smooth on an LED panel. Either way the clock always shows the right time: below that the program gives up rain and snow in motion, cloud and water motion, seconds, then draws one picture a minute, then the glass, the landscape and the sky become solid digits, a flat ground and a gradient (the Raspberry Pi program; a browser always draws everything).
.TP
.B bodySize
Sun & moon size (advanced). Values: 1 | 2 | 3. Default: 2. sun & moon size multiplier.
.TP
.B nightBrightness
Night brightness (advanced). Values: 0.5 to 4. Default: 1.4.
.TP
.B lightPollution
Light pollution (advanced). Values: auto | off | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9. Default: auto. auto (by time zone) | off | 1..9 (Bortle).
.TP
.B viewMode
Mode. Values: fixed | drag | look. Default: drag. fixed | drag (look around) | look (gyro "VR" mode). Needs motion sensors: web page only.
.TP
.B followSun
Follow the sun. Values: on | off. Default: on. clock view only: sun rises on the right quarter, sets on the left, tilt never changes.
.TP
.B showLabels
Label the sun, moon and planets (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: off.
.TP
.B viewHeading
Facing (advanced). Values: 0 to 359. Default: 180.
.TP
.B viewPitchAuto
Keep the horizon on the digits (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: on. keep the horizon on the clock digits.
.TP
.B horizonInDigits
Ground inside the digits (advanced). Values: 0 to 0.8. Default: 0.3. how far up the digits the horizon sits (0 = bottom edge): ground shows through the lower part.
.TP
.B viewPitch
Tilt up (advanced). Values: \-10 to 80. Default: 12.
.TP
.B viewFov
Field of view (advanced). Values: 30 to 110. Default: 80.
.TP
.B sensorRotation
Screen rotation (advanced). Values: auto | ignore. Default: auto. auto | ignore. Needs motion sensors: web page only.
.TP
.B compassRef
Compass reference (iPhone & iPad) (advanced). Values: auto | cam | top. Default: auto. auto | cam | top (iOS compass heading reference). Needs motion sensors: web page only.
.TP
.B vrDebug
Show sensor readout (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: off. settings panel. Needs motion sensors: web page only.
.SS Weather
.TP
.B weatherMode
Weather. Values: live | clear | partly | cloudy | overcast | rain | storm | snow | fog | haze. Default: live. live | clear | partly | cloudy | overcast | rain | storm | snow | fog | haze.
.TP
.B tempUnit
Temperature (advanced). Values: auto | c | f. Default: auto. auto (by region) | c | f.
.TP
.B cloudMotion
Cloud & water motion (advanced). Values: 1 | 0.25 | 0. Default: 1. 1 real time, 0.25 slow, 0 still. Needs two or more cores.
.TP
.B rainAlert
Umbrella alert. Values: on | off. Default: off. show an umbrella / slicker indicator when enough rain is coming today.
.TP
.B digitWeather
Rain and snow on the digits (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: on. on | off: rain beads and splashes, snow settling on the digits (glass, tube and LED styles). Needs an OpenGL ES 2 or 3 GPU (any Pi).
.TP
.B windSway
Wind sway (advanced). Values: off | lean | full. Default: off. off | lean | full: the digits lean downwind like palm trees (steady lean, or lean and gusts). Needs two or more cores.
.SS Extras
.TP
.B countdown
Countdown timer. Values: off | both | sunrise | sunset. Default: off. off | both | sunrise | sunset.
.TP
.B countdownKind
Count down to (advanced). Values: sun | golden | civil | nautical | astro | moon. Default: sun. sun | golden | civil | nautical | astro | moon: what the countdown counts down to (morning and evening events).
.TP
.B countdownLead
Start counting (advanced). Values: 10 | 15 | 20 | 30. Default: 20. minutes before the event the countdown appears.
.TP
.B brightnessDay
By day. Values: 0.1 to 1. Default: 1. 0.1 .. 1: how bright the screen is by day (1 = no veil).
.TP
.B brightnessNight
At night. Values: 0.1 to 1. Default: 1. 0.1 .. 1: how bright it is at night.
.TP
.B brightnessTransition
The change takes (advanced). Values: 15 | 30 | 45 | 60 | 90 | 120. Default: 45. minutes the change takes, centred on sunset and on sunrise.
.TP
.B screenMode
Look of the screen (advanced). Values: normal | led. Default: normal. normal | led (LED panel simulator).
.TP
.B ledCols
LEDs across (advanced). Values: 8 to 256. Default: 64. LEDs across the panel (64 x 32 is the classic panel).
.TP
.B ledRows
LEDs down (advanced). Values: 8 to 256. Default: 32. LEDs down it.
.TP
.B ledStars
Stars on the LED panel (advanced). Values: auto | always | off. Default: auto. off | auto | always: stars, planets and the moon that show in the normal picture also light an LED on the LED panel.
.TP
.B ledTurn
Turn to match the screen (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: on. turn the panel on its side when the screen is the other way round.
.TP
.B keepAwake
Keep the screen on. Values: on | off. Default: on. Screen Wake Lock.
.TP
.B antiBurnIn
Anti burn\-in (advanced). Values: auto | on | off. Default: auto. auto (while the screen is kept on) | on | off: step the digits a few pixels round a small square, once a minute.
.SS Place
.TP
.B preciseLocation
Use precise location. Values: on | off. Default: off.
.TP
.B manualLocation
Set the place myself. Values: on | off. Default: off. the place was typed or searched for (Settings \-> Place): never replaced by GPS or the time\-zone estimate.
.TP
.B timeZone
Show the time in another time zone. Values: text, up to 40 characters. Default: . an IANA time zone name ("America/New_York"); empty = this device's own time. Share links carry it as their own field (version 2), like the place.
.TP
.B gpsFrequency
Location update frequency (advanced). Values: \-1 | 1 | 5 | 15 | 30 | 60 | 120 | 720 | 1440 | \-2. Default: \-1.
.TP
.B coarseLookups
Share only an approximate position (advanced). Values: on | off. Default: on. weather / terrain lookups use a rounded position, never the exact one.
.SS Native only
.TP
.B location_latitude
Latitude. Values: \-90 to 90. Default: 0.
.TP
.B location_longitude
Longitude. Values: \-180 to 180. Default: 0.
.TP
.B kiosk
Sign mode. Values: on | off. Default: off.
.TP
.B output
Output. Values: hdmi | matrix. Default: hdmi.
.TP
.B matrixConfig
Panel layout file (matrix.cfg). Values: text, up to 120 characters. Default: .
.TP
.B renderScale
Draw HDMI this many times smaller (0 = automatic: smaller when a frame takes too long). Values: 0 to 8. Default: 0.
.TP
.B gamma
Gamma for LED panels. Values: 1 to 3. Default: 2.2.
.TP
.B ledGpioMapping
How the panels are wired to the Pi (led\-gpio\-mapping). Values: regular | adafruit\-hat | adafruit\-hat\-pwm. Default: regular.
.TP
.B ledSlowdownGpio
GPIO slowdown (led\-slowdown\-gpio): 1 to 4 on a Pi 3 and later. Values: 0 to 4. Default: 1.
.TP
.B ledPwmBits
Colour depth in bits (led\-pwm\-bits). Values: 1 to 11. Default: 11.
.TP
.B ledPwmLsbNanoseconds
Shortest pulse in nanoseconds (led\-pwm\-lsb\-nanoseconds). Values: 50 to 3000. Default: 130.
.TP
.B ledRgbSequence
Colour order of the panel (led\-rgb\-sequence). Values: text, up to 3 characters. Default: RGB.
.TP
.B ledPanelType
Panel chip (led\-panel\-type), for example FM6126A. Values: text, up to 12 characters. Default: .
.TP
.B ledMultiplexing
Row multiplexing (led\-multiplexing). Values: 0 to 17. Default: 0.
.TP
.B ledRowAddrType
Row address type (led\-row\-addr\-type). Values: 0 to 5. Default: 0.
.SH PRESETS
Applied with \fBwobbly\-clock preset\fR. A preset sets the look and the power settings; it never changes the place, units or labels.
.TP
.B standard
Standard. The default look: liquid glass, a live sky, following the sun.
.TP
.B bedside
Bedside. Calm and dim at night: no seconds, soft glow, slow clouds, screen stays on.
.TP
.B sunwatch
Sunset watcher. Countdowns to sunrise and sunset, with a touch more glow.
.TP
.B led
LED panel. 64 × 32 LED matrix with the countdown in pixels. Light on the battery.
.TP
.B weather
Weather watch. Umbrella alert and sunrise / sunset countdowns.
.TP
.B everyday
Everyday. Bedside calm plus the weather watch: no seconds, soft glow, dims at night, screen on, umbrella alert, sunrise and sunset countdowns.
.TP
.B everyday\-saver
Everyday, power saver. Everyday as an LED panel with every battery\-saver setting: still sky, flat colour, no plants, low quality, dimmer at night. The screen stays on, because it is a clock.
.TP
.B showcase
Showcase. Everything turned up: high quality, glowing glass, moving clouds.
.TP
.B saver
Battery saver. Still sky, flat ink, no plants, dimmed at night, screen not forced on.
.SH HARDWARE
Raspberry Pi Zero / Zero W: OpenGL ES 2 (the shaders have an ES 2 form); Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W: OpenGL ES 2 (the shaders have an ES 2 form); Raspberry Pi 3: OpenGL ES 2 (the shaders have an ES 2 form); Raspberry Pi 4: OpenGL ES 3; Raspberry Pi 5: OpenGL ES 3.
.SH SEE ALSO
wobbly\-clock(1)
